  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The framework's evaluation is limited to coasting intervals on two specific UK mainline rail corridors.",
      "what": "The study introduces a hybrid MAUKF-LSTM framework that combines a Mass-Adaptive Unscented Kalman Filter with a Long Short-Term Memory network to estimate freight train mass and running resistance in real time. Using timestamped position records from coasting intervals on two major UK mainline routes (Peterborough–Doncaster and Rugby–Crewe), the model separates mass from resistance by reformulating the Davis equation and training on a physics-informed loss function. The framework achieves relative mass errors of approximately 2% on the calibration route and under 1% on an unseen route.",
      "why": "It enables accurate, real-time estimation of critical dynamic train parameters using standard position data, eliminating the need for expensive, dedicated onboard mass-measurement hardware."
    }
  },
